"I wrote the coverage report to /tmp/claude-1000/-home-zhengyew-telelean/20626c17-0334-4498-ad86-9dc24b7010ed/scratchpad/plans/coverage_audit.md. It is the only file I wrote; nothing was published or built. A script check of the matrix confirmed that every per-section and total count in the summary matches the rows.\n\n**Counts.** The 873 mapper rows became 830 requirements, because 82 duplicate Appendix A rows were merged into 39 lines.\n\n| Status | Requirements | Share |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| built | 297 | 35.8 % |\n| planned slice 2 | 231 | 27.8 % |\n| planned slice 3 | 152 | 18.3 % |\n| slice 4 | 73 | 8.8 % |\n| slice 5 | 15 | 1.8 % |\n| narrowed by decision | 46 | 5.5 % |\n| contradicted | 11 | 1.3 % |\n| unassigned | 4 | 0.5 % |\n| out of scope | 1 | 0.1 % |\n\nOf the 17 gap candidates, 15 rows are real gaps, which come to 13 distinct issues: 2 for slice 2, 6 for slice 3, and 5 that need a decision logged. The other 2 are not gaps:\n- §14 item 2 bullet 4 (\"named in report\") is already covered by built code, so it now counts as built.\n- S20 (\"future work\", the consistency check) is M3 work, so it is out of scope.\n\n**Real gaps**\n- **G1 (slice 2, 2f), §14.2 bullet 1:** once a session is applied, nothing durable records that an arrow came from Claude. Apply should record each accepted Add arrow and Add premise arrow with its run and step.\n- **G2 (slice 2, plan fix), §14.9 apply and AR-3:** a hand-written cycle outside the question blocks neither Formalize nor Apply. Plan2 §4.12 check 6 should say \"any cycle in the subject blocks Formalize\".\n- **G3 (slice 3, fix the plan now), CM-3 freeze actions:** plan3 freezes only the freezable part of a selection and never shows you the rest (`left`). Either disable the action with the reasons, or log a decision that the result names every item left out.\n- **G4 (slice 3, 3b and 3f), ES-9 bullet 5 and S9:** \"Delete card only, keep Lean\" still exists end to end and leaves an unmarked axiom behind. Remove it, including keepLean, and update the user guide.\n- **G5 (slice 3, 3b; slice 4 too), CF-6:** when you edit a sentence Claude wrote, it stays marked as Claude's (worded_by: agent). The edit should set worded_by: user in the same Undo step.\n- **G6 (slice 3, 3f and 3b), AR-7 bullet 4:** the drop zone and Move to axioms should name the frozen arrows they remove. Kind changes and an arrow that replaces a frozen mark should also drop the matching freeze records.\n- **G7 (slice 3, 3f), BD-7 bullet 6:** the band names definitions in a tooltip, taken from the target's own statement only. It should be a chip, drawing on direct(v) and the proof's own lemmas too.\n- **G8 (slice 3, 3f), CM-7 bullet 4b:** the Vocabulary/Definitions band still opens VS Code's context menu. Extend telelean's menu to the band, or log a decision.\n- **G9 (decision), BD-3 and B.7:** the A|P box stores the new card's position, and kind changes and deletes drop stored positions. Log an AP entry, and correct AP-19 and docs/user-guide.md:66.\n- **G10 (decision, or a fix folded into G9), AR-6 bullet 1:** an axiom that becomes a proposition is placed by the general layout, not next to its new source.\n- **G11 (decision plus a cheap fix), A19:** an old axiom's pre-v4 arrows are not drawn at all. Log it, and name the source cards in the chip's tooltip.\n- **G12 (decision), CM-3 built menus:** with a mixed selection, actions act on the part they fit instead of being shown disabled. Log this rule.\n- **G13 (decision: keep the code), §14.2 bullet 4:** the signature leaves out subject-module axioms of kind `other`. This is stricter than the spec and fails closed; log it.\n\n**Slice 4 (transform window): 73 requirements**\n- **Core:** all of §8 TR (38) and ES-3 (5).\n- **The window's freezes:** the `revalue` hook, the `transform` reason, freezing inside the window, and the banner.\n- **Opening and session flow:** the Transform cards… button and action, UN-4 4a/4b, ES-6 drafts surviving a reload, ES-9 bullet 3, RV-5/7/8/9/12, DO-2, EN-2 Apply bullet 2.\n- **Elsewhere:** B.3 and the baseline rows in Appendix B, §14 item 10, S8–S11, the CF-1 and CF-4 transform rows, §1 Fuzzy and Transform.\n- **Follow-ups:**\n  - The slice-4 halves of G5 and G6.\n  - D3-43's fallback may move \"Claude may add cards\" here.\n  - D2-13's \"Ask me instead\" should become a Transform decline.\n  - D2-15 (no Shaky splits) stays unless reversed.\n  - D3-1's session-start freezes only become real in Transform sessions.\n  - TR-4's fuzzy Dependencies, TR-8 and TR-10 (c) need # references from slice 5, or a stub.\n\n**Slice 5 (references): 15 requirements.** RF-1 to RF-5 (10), §1 Reference, CF-1's # reference, CM-4's Copy reference, and FZ-4 bullet 2 with S12 (references hold their targets; plan3's heldFields() hook currently returns nothing). RF-2 (b), \"ids are never reused\", is already at risk in slice 3: ids are sentence slugs and standing freezes are keyed by id (D3-16), so a deleted card's freeze record could attach to a new card with the same sentence."